{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962274,"nonce":"uwR6girGlEfzEJ6VEUEuJmGbiJ8=","title":"Secondary windows never drain property updates, and node ids collide across trees","message":"Found by reading the code, not reproduced at runtime.\n\nPartial property updates go through one process-global queue\n(PENDING_PARTIAL_PROP_UPDATES, stateful.rs:451) of PartialPropertyUpdate\nrecords keyed by LayoutNodeId alone, and bindings are keyed the same way.\nLayoutNodeId is a key into each LayoutTree's own slotmap (tree.rs:213, 235),\nso ids repeat across trees.\n\n- The primary window drains the whole queue, twice per frame, into its own\n  RenderTree without filtering (windowed.rs:5745-5768, 5857-5870).\n- Secondary windows (secondary_windows, windowed.rs:2951-2954, built from\n  RenderTree::from_element at 3325-3328, which registers bindings via\n  div.rs:5006-5008) never drain it.\nSo a binding on a secondary window's node writes into whichever primary\nnode shares its key.\n\nSeparately, replacing or dropping a tree never unregisters its bindings:\nthe secondary rebuild (3328), the primary resize rebuild (6189-6215) and\nwindow close (3177). Stale subscribers leak and can alias nodes of the new\ntree.\n\nProposed fix (moderate, about 150-250 lines over about 10 files):\n- a TreeId on LayoutTree minted from a global atomic;\n- a tree field on PartialPropertyUpdate and on binding Subscriber, with\n  by_node keyed by (TreeId, LayoutNodeId);\n- `_in_tree` variants of queue_prop_update_partial (callers binding.rs:714,\n  stateful.rs:984), queue_layout_update_partial (binding.rs:723) and\n  register_typed* (binding.rs:401, 410, 476, 485, single caller div.rs:5007,\n  which already has the tree), keeping the old signatures as wrappers;\n- filter at every drain: windowed.rs (2), ios.rs:1346, web.rs:2669 and 2869,\n  android.rs:1537; drain in the secondary-window path;\n- unregister a tree's bindings when it is dropped or replaced.","files":null}]}